The removal ledger goes in the PR body, and a summary on this bead. rf2-3h7v2.8 (PR #10651) is a good model, including its scoped-build cross-check.

## Ruling

Fresco (`re-frame.fresco`, alias `h`) is re-frame2's taught default view layer for new applications. Reagent stays first-class as the tier for v1 migration and Reagent compatibility, and as the JVM-renderable SSR route. UIx stays first-class as the React- and hooks-first tier. Both remain explicit, supported scaffold choices. This bead carries the scaffold half of that ruling. When rf2-8urba's `:fresco` variant lands, the template's default `:substrate` flips from `:reagent` to `:fresco` in the same PR, the setup skill follows it, and the emitted Fresco counter is proved end to end, so the advertised default is one working greenfield path rather than a project that has to be migrated straight away.

Decided 2026-10-16: Mike directed that every dossier recommendation an independent Codex review agreed with be actioned. Mike's instruction, verbatim:

> review all decisions. They now have a "Codex Recomendation" section.  Where the original recomendation matches the Code Recomendation, create a bead to action the decision.  And then remove the file.  Leave behind cases where the two differ materially.

The original recommendation is "(A), Fresco is the taught default, ruled now". The scaffold default flips in the PR that lands rf2-8urba's `:fresco` variant, and the setup skill's first-counter leaf moves with it. Codex: "Choose Fresco as the taught path for new applications organised around re-frame2, and keep Reagent and UIx as explicit, supported choices. Decide that direction now, then switch the advertised default through one working greenfield path." Codex's smallest action is to add the Fresco scaffold variant and exercise its emitted counter, then align the AI setup references. Both condition the ruling on SSR in the same way, set out below.

Decisive facts, at trunk 89517e8f54:
1. `tools/template/src/day8/re_frame2_template/hooks.clj:40` is `(def ^:private default-substrate :reagent)`, and the registry at `:35-36` holds only `:reagent` and `:uix`.
2. `skills/re-frame2-setup/SKILL.md:54` tells an AI pair "Reagent is the default substrate … Fresco … is not a scaffold option … a greenfield project starts on an adapter and moves later if it wants to". The default path therefore sends every new app through a later migration.
3. SSR is the one real cost. `implementation/fresco/src/re_frame/fresco.cljc:76-81`: Fresco's `:clj` side is three macros, and "there is no JVM render path". Fresco renders on the server through Node only, so a JVM (Ring) backend that wants SSR of Fresco views needs the documented Node crossing (`docs/ssr/concepts.md:739-745`). Reagent hiccup stays JVM-renderable. Both recommendations hold that if Mike ever rules Node-free JVM SSR a primary requirement of the default path, Reagent should stay the default instead.

Rejected options:
- (B) Fresco as an optional module with Reagent the default permanently. The project would maintain a full in-house view runtime that it does not teach, against HD-029, "Fresco graduates, as a success" (`docs/design/fresco/decisions.md:2906`).
- (C) Gating the ruling on the counted pilots (rf2-hic-063). The pilots measure unaided adoption, not Fresco against Reagent, so a pass is consistent with either answer, and they sit behind a publication chain that has not moved in two months.

Reopen conditions, recorded with the ruling:
- a real greenfield workflow failure on the emitted Fresco scaffold, or a counted pilot needing framework-author help for an architectural reason (not documentation or packaging);
- Mike ruling that Node-free JVM SSR is a primary requirement of the default path;
- the K1 price record lapsing, with the canonical mount row above 1.25× (`docs/design/fresco/product/k1-price-acceptance.md` §7);
- K2 crossing its 1.5× architecture kill.

A revert is one constant plus the template and setup-skill prose that states it.

Supersedes, in rf2-8urba:
- its "Reagent stays the default" clause (the axis ruling of 2026-09-02, reaffirmed 2026-09-09);
- its rejection of "D (Fresco as the default)";
- its out-of-scope line "Not making Fresco the default substrate. Separate bead, gated on pilot evidence".

This is that separate bead, filed without the pilot gate. rf2-8urba's `:substrate` axis (one selector, now three values) and its hold on publication STAND.

## Work

This lands in the same PR as rf2-8urba's `:fresco` variant (its `_fresco/` tree, registry entry and `case` arm). It does not duplicate that work.

- `tools/template/src/day8/re_frame2_template/hooks.clj:40`: set `default-substrate` to `:fresco`. `:reagent` and `:uix` stay selectable and unchanged.
- Template prose that states the default:
  - `tools/template/resources/day8/re_frame2_template/template.edn:6` (the description string);
  - `tools/template/README.md:67` ("# Reagent — the default");
  - `tools/template/spec/001-Substrate-Variants.md:9-14`, `:30` and `:56` (`(coerce-substrate nil)` now returns `:fresco`);
  - `tools/template/spec/API.md:36`, `:48` and `:79`;
  - `tools/template/spec/DESIGN-RATIONALE.md` wherever it states the default.
- Template tests:
  - `tools/template/test/day8/re_frame2_template/template_test.clj:19` and `:295` (`reagent-is-the-default-test`) become a Fresco-is-the-default test;
  - the setup-skill default-scaffold fixture in `emitted_test_run_test.clj:747-860` follows the new default.
- `skills/re-frame2-setup/`:
  - `SKILL.md:54` cardinal rule 3: Fresco is the default, and Reagent and UIx are explicit swaps;
  - step 1's swap note (`:84`) and step 2's `:local/root` coordinates (`:85`), which name `implementation/adapters/reagent`;
  - `references/first-counter.md`, which is drift-locked to the template's default emission, so regenerate it from the new default;
  - `references/entry-namespace.md`, where Reagent greenfield becomes a swap section beside UIx greenfield;
  - `spec/design.md` wherever it states the default.
- **The SSR choice before installation.** One paragraph in the template README and one in the setup skill, placed ahead of the install steps. It says that Fresco renders on the server through Node only, and that an app wanting SSR from a JVM host without Node should take `:substrate :reagent`. Prose only, no new machinery.
- `docs/core/fresco/00-installation.md:9-10`: rf2-8urba already rewrites "scaffolds `:reagent` and `:uix` projects only". State here that the template's default is Fresco.
- **Prove the emitted Fresco counter end to end** before advertising it. Run through install, compile, the starter test, a controlled-field change (add or edit a `views.cljs` input bound to app-db and confirm it updates), hot reload, and a production `release` build. The nightly emitted-app smoke covers resolve, compile and boot. Record the hand-run steps and their results in the PR body. Fix any packaging friction this run turns up in the same PR, or file it.
- Deliberately stays; these belong to the half of the dossier still open for Mike (the timing and scope of the docs path, a `spec/004-Views.md`, and example conversion):
  - the Views chapter (`docs/core/views.md`);
  - `skills/re-frame2`'s view references;
  - `examples/`;
  - Spec 006's "Reagent as default adapter" wording (`spec/006-ReactiveSubstrate.md:1429`, `:1930`);
  - `README.md:184`'s "(browser default)";
  - the Architecture Overview line in `CLAUDE.md`.

  Do not edit them here, but list in the PR body any that this flip leaves contradicting the template.

## Sequencing

- Held with rf2-8urba on publication: rf2-uelji, then rf2-fo4ng, then rf2-kmqx3 (the first `v*` tag). Lands in the SAME PR as rf2-8urba (and after its prerequisite rf2-ps1u). Depends on the sibling bead from the same dossier that puts Fresco's test kit on the artefact's `:paths`.
- Hot zones: none of CLAUDE.md's list, unless `expensive-tests.yml`'s `timeout-minutes` budget has to move for the emitted-app smoke. That would be `.github/workflows/*` and gets its own one-line PR, per rf2-8urba. `tools/template/**` sequences against rf2-fo4ng (which rewrites every coordinate in that tree) and rf2-j908 (the `_uix` variant repair), per rf2-8urba.
- Cross-dossier:
  - Under this ruling, the Node render route becomes the default path to SSR. Work from `node-ssr-allowlist-and-html-string.md` that changes the Node SSR recipe the template README points at should land before this, or with it.
  - `reagent-slim-keep-or-retire.md` is informed by this ruling but is not ordered against it.
  - The still-open half of `fresco-taught-default-or-optional.md` (the docs path, 004 and examples) is ordered against this bead in whichever direction Mike rules.

